{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T17:24:49.980Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work:\n\n**Accepted all six acceptance lines.**\n\n## Changed\n- `src/commands/reconcile.ts`\n  - Replaced the `--redeploy` selection: instead of scanning current-plan `fail` items, it now walks `listApps` (name order) and picks each app with no running deployment left after the plan whose latest deployment is either (a) failed by this run's plan for a container reason, or (b) `failed` with `running` in its status history. Health failures and stuck deployments are excluded.\n  - Removed the module-level `WeakMap`; added `name: string | null` to `ReportItem` (human-only).\n  - Added `jsonReport` projection so `--json` items keep exactly `{kind, app, deploymentId, containerId, detail, ok}`.\n- `tests/reconcile-redeploy-cli.test.ts` (new)\n  - Copies helpers from `tests/reconcile-cli.test.ts` (no imports), seeds a health failure via `FakeRuntime` script `exitCode: 3`, and covers earlier-run failures, dry run, health failure, stopped/stuck apps, name ordering, orphan/prune names, the `name` field, six JSON keys, and no `WeakMap`.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/reconcile-redeploy-cli.test.ts` → 9/9 pass (exit 0)\n- `pnpm verify` → tsc clean, 382/382 tests pass, including the two frozen suites\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/012-first-real-deploy/.run/results/1.md`.\n\nTouched: src/commands/reconcile.ts, tests/reconcile-redeploy-cli.test.ts"}}
